'''Laguna's 4th congressional district''' is one of the seven [[congressional districts of the Philippines]] in the province of [[Laguna (province)|Laguna]]. It has been represented in the [[House of Representatives of the Philippines]] since 1987.<ref name="congleg">{{cite web|url=http://www.congress.gov.ph/legislators/?v=province |title=Roster of Philippine legislators |publisher=[[House of Representatives of the Philippines]] |accessdate=February 7, 2021}}</ref> The district consists of the capital municipality of [[Santa Cruz, Laguna|Santa Cruz]] and the entire eastern Laguna municipalities of [[Cavinti]], [[Famy, Laguna|Famy]], [[Kalayaan, Laguna|Kalayaan]], [[Luisiana, Laguna|Luisiana]], [[Lumban]], [[Mabitac]], [[Magdalena, Laguna|Magdalena]], [[Majayjay]], [[Paete]], [[Pagsanjan]], [[Pakil]], [[Pangil]], [[Pila, Laguna|Pila]], [[Santa Maria, Laguna|Santa Maria]] and [[Siniloan]].<ref name="apportion">{{cite web|url=https://www.chanrobles.com/ordinance.htm |title=The 1987 Constitution of the Republic of the Philippines |publisher=Chan Robles Virtual Law Library |accessdate=February 7, 2021}}</ref> It is currently represented in the [[20th Congress of the Philippines|20th Congress]] by [[Benjamin Agarao Jr.]] of the [[Partido Federal ng Pilipinas]].<ref name="congmem">{{cite web|url=http://www.congress.gov.ph/members/ |title=House Members |publisher=[[House of Representatives of the Philippines]] |accessdate=February 7, 2021}}</ref>

